# Pekit build artifacts: per-recipe staging trees and release-worktree links
# to a shared staging tree. As with the repository link below, omit the trailing
# slash so a cache-sharing symlink cannot dirty exact package provenance.
out
_pkgsOut_
# Also match a release worktree's symlink to the shared repository. A trailing
# slash ignores only real directories; leaving it off keeps that operational
# symlink from falsely marking otherwise exact-commit package provenance dirty.
_peipkgRepo_
_pkgsOut_.presigning-bak/
# Legacy publish-pool name (superseded by _pkgsOut_/); never commit the pool.
pkgsOut/
# Dated/labelled snapshots of the pool taken before a sweeping change
# (_pkgsOut_.pre-pfsl-…, .pre-hardening-bak, .superseded). Same artifacts, same
# reason, and they run to gigabytes: three of them were 3.1 GB and one
# `git add -A` away from the history.
_pkgsOut_.*/

# Keyring files are per-developer / environment-specific (hold or reference key
# material) and are never committed.
*.keyring.pekit.toml
# ...and their backups. The pattern above is anchored at the end, so a .bak
# suffix slips past it while holding exactly the same key material.
*.keyring.pekit.toml.*

# Milestone-2 toolchain build scratch: the build-only nix->peios cross toolchain
# (gcc/_cross/tools) + its build tree (gcc/_cross/build), and the peipkg-compose'd
# sysroot (gcc/_sysroot). The driving scripts gcc/_cross/*.sh ARE tracked.
gcc/_cross/tools/
gcc/_cross/build/
gcc/_sysroot/
# peipkg-compose lock: regenerated per machine; pins absolute local out/ paths.
sysroot.lock.toml

# Local dev package-signing key material (PEI-154); never commit.
/dev-signing.key
/dev-signing.pub
